    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incŏhĭbĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		in-cohibeo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that cannot be held</i> or <i>kept
				together</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illo genere oneris tam impedito ac tam
					incohibili,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					5, 3, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That cannot be restrained</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cursus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 24, 1, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ardor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 14, 2</span></i>
			. </div>
